node_modules/
# dist/ is intentionally COMMITTED: this package is consumed by apps as a git
# submodule (no npm registry), so the prebuilt, self-contained bundle must ship
# in-repo for zero-config, zero-build drop-in. Rebuild (`npm run build`) + commit
# dist on every source change so consuming apps pick it up on their next release.
